# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, 4-component with the min-max stage.
#
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION first minimizes over the positive-energy spinors only (no-pair approximation, the
# negative-energy branch excluded from the rotations). FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE then continues from that
# minimum with rotations that also mix the occupied positive-energy spinors with the negative-energy ones:
# NEO drives the orbitals to the saddle point (energy maximized along the electron-positron rotations, minimized
# along the rest -- Talman 1986, Saue 2011), and the occupation numbers are re-minimized, macro-iterated.
# The log gives the order of the saddle (from the occupations > 1e-6), the check that the rotated integrals
# reproduce the first stage's energy, and the block-wise Hessian check at the end.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
